stem_md:
A polynomial  $p$  can be written as 
\begin{align*}
p(x) = x^6+3x^5-3x^4+ax^3+bx^2+cx+d.
\end{align*}
Given that all roots of  $p(x)$  are equal to either  $m$  or  $n$  where  $m$  and  $n$  are integers, compute  $p(2)$ .

A sequence of real numbers  $\{a_n\}_{n = 1}^\infty (n=1,2,...)$  has the following property:
\begin{align*}
6a_n+5a_{n-2}=20+11a_{n-1}\  (\text{for }n\geq3).
\end{align*}
The first two elements are  $a_1=0, a_2=1$ . Find the integer closest to  $a_{2011}$ .

If we define  $\otimes(a,b,c)$  by
\begin{align*}
\otimes(a,b,c) = \frac{\max(a,b,c)- \min(a,b,c)}{a+b+c-\min(a,b,c)-\max(a,b,c)},
\end{align*}
compute  $\otimes(\otimes(7,1,3),\otimes(-3,-4,2),1)$ .

