- $O_1, O_2$  = centers of  $\gamma_1, \gamma_2$ ;  $U_1, U_2$  = tangency points on  $KL$ ;  $T_1, T_2$  = tangency points on  $(ABC)$
- $Q$  = midpoint of  $\widehat{BAC}$
- $M_1, M_2$  = midpoints of  $T_1U_1, T_2U_2$
- $S = U_1U_2 \cap O_1O_2$
- $X = U_1T_2 \cap U_2T_1$

We claim that the locus is the bisector of  $\angle{BAC}$ .**<span style="color:#00f">Claim 1:</span>**  $Q = T_1U_1 \cap T_2U_2$ , and  $T_1U_1U_2T_2$  is cyclic.
The former is true by homothety at  $T_1, T_2$  taking  $\gamma_1, \gamma_2$  to  $(ABC)$ , and the latter because  $\triangle{QU_1K} \sim \triangle{QKT_1} \implies QU_1 \cdot QT_1 = QK^2 = QL^2 = QU_2 \cdot QT_2$ .**<span style="color:#00f">Claim 2:</span>**  $MY, MS$  are internal and external bisectors of  $\angle{O_1MO_2}$ .
First, by Monge on  $\gamma_1, \gamma_2, (ABC)$ ,  $S, T_1, T_2$  are collinear, thus  $S$  is the exsimilicenter and if  $Y$  is the insimilicenter then  $S, O_1, Y, O_2$  is harmonic. By Brocard,  $O$  is the orthocenter of  $\triangle{XSQ}$ , and if  $M$  is the foot of the altitude from  $O$  to  $QS$  then  $S, T_1, QX \cap T_1T_2, T_2$  is harmonic. Projecting from  $Q$  onto  $(OQ)$ ,  $M, M_1, QX \cap (OQ), M_2$  is harmonic, and finally projecting from  $O$  onto  $O_1O_2$ , we get that  $O, Y, X, M$  are collinear, and since  $\angle{SMY} = 90^{\circ}$ ,  $MY$  bisects  $\angle{O_1MO_2}$ .

Clearly  $MY$  passes through the antipode of  $Q$  wrt  $(ABC) \implies MO_1, MO_2 \cap (ABC)$  lie on a line parallel to  $BC$ , and  $\frac{MO_1}{MO_2} = \frac{O_1U_1}{O_2U_2} \implies$  the tangents from  $M$  to  $\gamma_1, \gamma_2$  intersect  $(ABC)$  at points which are reflections over the perp bisector of  $BC \implies M = A$ , and the insimilicenter  $Y$  does indeed lie on the  $A$ -bisector.  $\square$

