    &= (a+b)^2 + (b+c)^2 + (c+a)^2. 
\end{align*}
Let  $x = a+b, y = b+c, z = c+a$ .  Then the given condition is equivalent to  $x^2+y^2+z^2 \le 4$  which implies  $4 - y^2 - z^2 \ge x^2.$  

Also note that  $a = \frac{x - y + z}{2}, b = \frac{x + y - z}{2}, c = \frac{-x+y+z}{2}$ .  

Thus, we have 
\begin{align*}
