We will proceed with complex numbers. Let  $A,B,C,D,E \rightarrow a,b,c,d,e$ . WLOG, let  $(ABCDE)$  be the unit circle and  $b=1$ . Note that  $p=\frac{2d}{d+1}$ . Since  $P$ ,  $A$ , and  $C$  are collinear,  
\begin{align*}
\begin{vmatrix}
\frac{2d}{d+1} & \frac{2}{d+1} & 1 
a & \frac{1}{a} & 1 
c & \frac{1}{c} & 1 
\end{vmatrix}
=
0.
\end{align*}
Note that 
\begin{align*}
\begin{vmatrix}
\frac{2d}{d+1} & \frac{2}{d+1} & 1 
a & \frac{1}{a} & 1 
c & \frac{1}{c} & 1 
\end{vmatrix}
=
\frac{2d}{d+1}(\frac{c-a}{ac})-\frac{2}{d+1}(a-c)+\frac{(a-c)(a+c)}{ac}
=
0
\implies
\end{align*}
\begin{align*}
-2d-2ac+(a+c)(d+1)
=
0
\implies
(a+c)(d+1)
=
2ac+2d.
\end{align*}
Also note that  $e=\frac{ac}{d}$ . It is left to show
\begin{align*}
\begin{vmatrix}
1 & 1 & 1 
\frac{a+c}{2} & \frac{a+c}{2ac} & 1 
\frac{ac}{d} & \frac{d}{ac} & 1
\end{vmatrix}
=
0.
\end{align*}
\begin{align*}
\begin{vmatrix}
1 & 1 & 1 
\frac{a+c}{2} & \frac{a+c}{2ac} & 1 
\frac{ac}{d} & \frac{d}{ac} & 1
\end{vmatrix}
=
\frac{a+c}{2ac}-\frac{d}{ac}+\frac{ac}{d}-\frac{a+c}{2}+\frac{(a+c)d}{2ac}-\frac{a+c}{2d}
=
\frac{(a+c)(d+1)-2d}{2ac}+\frac{2ac}{2d}-\frac{(a+c)(d+1)}{2d}=1-\frac{2ac-(a+c)(d+1)}{2d}=0. 
\blacksquare
\end{align*}

Let  $AC \cap BE = X$ , and let  $O$  be the center of  $\omega$ . Since  $\triangle AOC$  is isosceles, it suffices to show that  $\overline{OX}$  is an altitude of  $\triangle AOC$ ; in particular, we show that  $\angle AXO = 90$ . First, since  $\angle OBP = 90 = \angle ODP$ , quadrilateral  $OBPD$  is cyclic. Noting that  $PX \parallel DE$ ,
\begin{align*}
\angle PXB = \angle DEB = \frac{1}{2} \angle DOB = \frac{1}{2} (180 - \angle DPB) = 90 - \angle OPB = \angle POB,
\end{align*}
so quadrilateral  $OXBP$  is cyclic. Thus,
\begin{align*}
\angle AXO = \angle PXO = \angle PBO = 90,
\end{align*}
as required.  $\square$

