Let the common value be  $k$ . Then,
\begin{align*}
x^k &= 4y^2
(2x)^k &= 16z^2
(2x^4)^k &= 8yz
\end{align*}
Multiplying the first and second and dividing by the square of the last we have,
\begin{align*}
\frac{x^k \cdot (2x)^k}{(2x^4)^{2k}} &= 1
\iff x^k \cdot (2x)^k &= (2x^4)^{2k}
\iff x \cdot (2x) &= (2x^4)^2
\end{align*} 
which yields  $2x^2 = 4x^8$  or  $x= \frac{1}{2^{\frac{1}{6}}}$ . Now we have,
\begin{align*}
2^{-\frac{k}{12} - 1} &= y
2^{\frac{k}{2} - \frac{k}{12} - 2} &= z
\end{align*} 
Then  $xy^5z = 2^{-\frac{43}{6}}$  which yields an answer of  $\boxed{049}$ .

