Let  $M$  be the midpoint of  $AB$ .  Extend  $DA$  to  $L$  so that  $AHBL$  is a rectangle. 
Then  $LHCD$  being an isosceles trapezium is cyclic. 
So, it is enough to show that  $LKHC$  is cyclic.
Choose a point  $P$  on  $CK$  such that  $APBK$  is a parallelogram.
Now,  $MA \cdot MB=MK \cdot MC$   $\Longrightarrow  MH^2=MP \cdot MC$   $\Longrightarrow \triangle MPH \sim \triangle MHC \Longrightarrow \angle MHP =\angle MCH=\theta$  (say).
Now,  $LPHK$  is a parallelogram  $\Longrightarrow \angle KLH=\angle MHP=\theta=\angle KCH \Longrightarrow$   $L$ ,  $K$ ,  $H$ ,  $C$  are concyclic  $\text{   } \square$ [asy]
