Summing and subtracting yields  $a_{n+1}+b_{n+1} = 2\left(a_n+b_n\right)$  and  $a_{n+1} - b_{n+1} = 2\sqrt{a_n^2+b_n^2}$ . Thus,
\begin{align*}
4a_{n+1}b_{n+1} = \left(a_{n+1}+b_{n+1}\right)^2 - \left(a_{n+1}-b_{n+1}\right)^2 = 8a_nb_n.
\end{align*}
So,  $a_{n+1}b_{n+1} = 2a_nb_n$ . 

We know that  $a_0+b_0 = -1 \cdot 2^0$ , so  $a_n+b_n = -1 \cdot 2^n$ . In addition,  $a_0b_0 = -1 \cdot 2^1$ , so  $a_nb_n = -1 \cdot 2^{n+1}$ . So,
\begin{align*}
a_n - b_n = \sqrt{\left(a_n + b_n\right)^2 - 4 \cdot a_nb_n} = \sqrt{2^{2n} + 2^{n+3}}.
\end{align*}
Therefore, we may conclude
\begin{align*}
a_n = \dfrac{\left(a_n+b_n\right) + \left(a_n - b_n\right)}{2} = \dfrac{\sqrt{2^{2n} + 2^{n+3}} - 2^n}{2}.
\end{align*}
Solving for  $n = 2012$  yields  $\boxed{2^{1006} \sqrt{2^{2000}+2}-2^{2011}}$ .

