    SM&=SB+BM=AB+BK=AK
    TM&=TC+CM=AC+CL=AL
\end{align*}
implying the desired (since  $AK$  and  $AL$  are equal tangents).

We claim that  $A, F, K, J, L, G$  are cyclic. For the proof notice that  $M$  is the orthocenter of triangle  $\triangle GFJ$ . Now
\begin{align*}
\angle JFL&=90^\circ -\angle CJB
&=90^\circ -\left(180^\circ -90^\circ +\frac{\angle B}{2}-90^\circ +\frac{\angle C}{2}\right)
&=90-\frac{1}{2}(\angle B+\angle C)
