k(y^2-yz+z^2)&=yz+1\end{align*}
However, if  $|y-z|> 1$ , then  $k(y^2-yz+z^2)\geq y^2-yz+z^2> yz+1$  therefore  $y=z$  or  $|y-z|=1$ .  The former produces  $2y^2=503y^2+503$  which makes  $503|y$  and so  $503^2||2y^2$  and  $503||503y^2+503=2y^2$ , a contradiction.  The latter makes  $k=1$  and produces the solution
